.TH MSHELL 1.SH NAMEmshell \- a menu shell.SH SYNOPSIS\fBmshell\fRmenufile.SH DESCRIPTION\fBmshell\fRshows a menu read from\fImenufile\fR,\fRone entry to a line written\fBlabel| command\fR,\fRup to ten of them, each label numbered on the screen.  Typing a numberruns that entry's command, then waits for RETURN and shows the menu again;a command ending in\fB&\fRruns in the background.  Anything after an\fB@\fRis a comment.  Control-C leaves..nf    Directory| dir    Extended directory| dir -e.fi.SH NOTESNeeds Microware's\fBcio\fR.\fRIt hands each command to a module called\fBshell\fR,\fRthe one your own OS-9 brings; load it first(\fBload /h1/CMDS/shell\fR).DOC/samples/menu is a menu to try..SH SEE ALSOgshell